<PARA INFOID = "T010039A131" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Valve Related Items</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>VVT-i (Variable Valve Timing-intelligent) has been adopted, which varies the intake valve timing according to driving conditions to achieve both low fuel consumption and high output as well as low emissions.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740031p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.403in" />
</FIGURE>

<MECA ID = "T010039A131A466" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "31Mar2004"     MECATYPE = "ACTUATE" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Valve, Valve Lifter and Valve Spring</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The intake valves and exhaust valves have been nitrided over their entire surface to ensure wear resistance. Also, weight has been reduced by making the stems smaller in diameter.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The exhaust valves have been heat treated (solution aging treatment) to cope with the rise in exhaust temperature due to higher performance.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Shimless type valve lifters with a large effective area have been adopted to accommodate high lift. Also, the top surface has been treated with Fericoat (molybdenum-containing iron phosphate coating) to ensure reliability and reduce friction.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The valve springs use high-strength material and are nitrided for higher strength, and have a thin wire diameter and uneven pitch to improve valve follow-up, achieve high lift and reduce weight.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740032p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.514in" />
</FIGURE>
